sg-mail (0.1.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Runs on Thunderbird 157 (Mozilla's official build, Stained Glass OS's
    thunderbird package from sg-image's thunderbird/) as on Debian's 140.
    Thunderbird 145+ sets accounts up in its Account Hub, a dialog over SG
    Mail's window (File > Add Account, and the first start without an
    account), which also offers Exchange (EWS) and Microsoft 365 (Microsoft
    Graph) mail accounts found by Autodiscover. Microsoft calendars: no
    Thunderbird release syncs them yet (README).
  * Gates: `make test TB_DEB=thunderbird_*.deb` runs every gate on that
    thunderbird package put over Debian's, in a root of its own (sg-image's
    release runs them on each new Thunderbird before taking it). look-gate
    follows whichever account setup comes up (the hub: autoconfig, account
    made, folder pane; Exchange and Graph offered; closing a tool tab comes
    back to SG Mail). All gates pass on 157 and look-gate on 140; the
    mutants on 157.

 -- Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0000

sg-mail (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First package: SG Mail, Stained Glass OS's mail and calendar, built on
    Debian's unmodified Thunderbird. /usr/bin/sg-mail runs Thunderbird with
    SG Mail's own profile; our extension (sg-mail@stained-glass-os.org)
    makes its main window SG Mail's: ribbon, folder pane with Favorites and
    unread counts, message list grouped by date, reading pane (HTML made
    safe, pictures from the network on request), message window (rich text,
    names from the address book, attachments, signatures, drafts, replies
    under Outlook-style headers), Calendar (Day / Work Week / Week / Month,
    appointments, recurrence, meetings and invitations, reminders as desktop
    notifications, .ics import/export), Outlook's keys, mailto: handler,
    light and dark. Gates: test/gate/*-gate.py with mutants (make test,
    make test-mutation).

 -- Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
